vayu: point the GPU at vayu's scanout buffer

A6_FB_PA was RMX1931's framebuffer (0x9d000000). vayu's ABL scans out from
cont_splash at 0x9c000000 (shim probe: VIG0 addr 0x9c000000, patch 0152), so
every GPU-presented frame went 16 MiB past the panel's buffer: the screen kept
the last CPU-drawn frame, read with the new 4352-byte rows, i.e. a frozen,
slanted progress bar. The stride latch itself works (shim stride test: CTL0
flush 0x3 is enough).


diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_a6xx.h b/bsd/dev/sweet_a6xx.h
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_a6xx.h
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_a6xx.h
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
 #define A6_RING_SIZE		0x8000u
 #define A6_RING_DW		(A6_RING_SIZE / 4)
 
-#define A6_FB_PA		0x9d000000ull
+#define A6_FB_PA		0x9c000000ull	/* vayu cont_splash scanout (RMX1931: 0x9d000000) */
 #define A6_FB_SIZE		0xa00000ull	/* mapped for the GPU: 5 x 2 MB */
 
 #define A6_GPU_ID		640
